Third-party material

This extension is a port of the simulator plugin bundled with Band (band-app/band, plugins/simulator,
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Band) and ships a copy of its extension worker SDK
(packages/extension-worker-sdk, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Band) as src/sdk/.

It ships these npm packages unmodified, in node_modules/:

- serve-sim 0.1.47, Apache License 2.0, Copyright Evan Bacon. https://github.com/EvanBacon/serve-sim
  Its dist/ holds the screen capture and input helpers (a native Node module and helper binaries)
  that this extension runs. They use Apple's private SimulatorKit and CoreSimulator APIs.
- ws 8, MIT License, Copyright (c) Einar Otto Stangvik and contributors. https://github.com/websockets/ws
- sharp 0.34, Apache License 2.0, Copyright Lovell Fuller and contributors. https://github.com/lovell/sharp
  The hub profile uses it to resize frames in process. It loads @img/sharp-darwin-arm64 and
  @img/sharp-darwin-x64 (Apache License 2.0) and the libvips builds in @img/sharp-libvips-darwin-arm64
  and @img/sharp-libvips-darwin-x64 (LGPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips). libvips
  is a separate dynamic library file in node_modules/@img/, so it can be replaced. Its dependencies
  @img/colour (MIT), detect-libc (Apache License 2.0) and semver (ISC) ship alongside.
